From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:20:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fade from the boot splash into the desktop without a
 black screen

After the disk is unlocked, Plymouth quits before sddm starts and the
screen stays pure black until the shell reveals the desktop: 4.50, 4.25
and 4.25 s on three reboots of quattro in QEMU, sampled every 250 ms.
Three things paint it black: plymouth-quit.service tears the splash
down first, Hyprland's background_color is black, and the shell's login
cover is a black rectangle.

sddm has no Plymouth handover of its own, so a drop-in gives it gdm's:
plymouth-quit.service is conflicted out and Plymouth is deactivated
instead, keeping its last frame on screen until Hyprland has committed
a buffer of its own to every output it enables at startup. Hyprland
then emits hyprland.start as it begins rendering (src/render/Renderer.cpp),
and the handler, the session's in autostart.lua or the greeter's in
default/sddm/hyprland.lua, starts omarchy-plymouth-quit.service, which
quits Plymouth with --retain-splash, through a sudoers grant for that
one command. sudo -n never prompts, so a machine without the grant
falls back to the timer, which quits Plymouth 60 s after sddm starts if
neither Hyprland does. A failed sddm still runs the plain quit through
OnFailure.

Plymouth has to go as soon as Hyprland has the display, not after the
shell: multi-user.target waits for plymouth-quit-wait.service and
power-profiles-daemon is ordered after multi-user.target, so a shell
that asked for power profiles before Plymouth quit sat out the 25 s
D-Bus timeout. Released from hyprland.start, Plymouth is gone 0.4 s
after Hyprland starts and before the shell launches.

The colours come from the splash itself. Hyprland, the greeter and the
login cover read the background Plymouth paints from the installed
omarchy.script and truncate it to 8 bits as Plymouth does: Plymouth
paints the stock 0.101, 0.105, 0.149 as #191a25, not #1a1b26. The
splash's logo stays with Plymouth; Hyprland draws frames of its own
before the cover maps, and a logo on the cover blinked out and back.

On the same three reboots with this change, the screen goes from the
splash to its own colour to the desktop, with one 250 ms sample of
black where Hyprland commits its first, still unrendered buffer
(src/output/Monitor.cpp, ensureBufferPresent). Unlock to wallpaper is
unchanged: 8.41, 8.44 and 8.38 s against 9.12, 8.37 and 8.39 s. A boot
with autologin off reaches the greeter the same way, its Hyprland
quitting Plymouth 0.6 s after it starts.

[J604: onto the 4.5.0 stable source ac2690cd. Conflict in
 shell/services/BackgroundIntro.qml resolved by keeping the stable side and
 adding only this commit's splashDir/splashBackground block; the other lines
 in that hunk (themeFinishing .. coverPresented) come from later quattro work
 that 4.5 does not carry. All other hunks applied as they are.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
